  <page>
    <title>Category:Items</title>
    <ns>14</ns>
    <id>2379</id>
    <revision><id>7830</id><timestamp>2026-01-01T16:13:17Z</timestamp><text>In PEAK, items are the objects you find while climbing that help you survive, heal, navigate, and overcome hazards. They include food and consumables (like granola bars, trail mix, energy drinks, and mushrooms that restore hunger/stamina or give buffs), climbing and utility equipment (such as rope spools, rope and anti-rope cannons, chain cannons, pitons, shelf shrooms, magic beans, lanterns, portable stoves, and compasses), healing and status items (like bandages, first-aid kits, antidotes, cure-alls, remedy fungus, heat packs, and faerie lanterns), as well as miscellaneous and collectible items (including Bing Bong, flying discs, scrolls/torn pages, balloons, blowguns, cursed skulls, scout effigies, and powerful relics like the Ancient Idol). These items are found in luggage, foraged from the environment, dropped by statues, or earned through exploration and are essential for managing hunger, stamina, status effects, and team support as you climb.

For food items specifically, click [[Food|here.]]</text></revision>
  </page>
  <page>
    <title>Category:Items that can be knocked down</title>
    <ns>14</ns>
    <id>2398</id>
    <revision><id>7894</id><timestamp>2026-01-03T05:57:44Z</timestamp><text>Items in this category can be knocked down by throwing an item at them or by using explosives. These items naturally spawn in the environment and can typically be found on trees, vines or cactus. Not all items found on plants can be knocked down.

Some of these items will transform into one or more other items e.g. Knocking down a {{Item|Coconut}} will yield 2 {{Item|Half-Coconut}}s.

&lt;!--
Items that cannot be knocked down based on testing using 1.51.a:
* Shroomberries, whether they be attached to the ground or a vine
* Kingberries
* Clusterberries
* Crispberries
* Napberry
* Aloe Vera
--&gt;</text></revision>
  </page>
  <page>
    <title>Category:Consumable</title>
    <ns>14</ns>
    <id>2399</id>
    <revision><id>7882</id><timestamp>2026-01-02T04:59:21Z</timestamp><text>In PEAK, consumables are single-use items that provide immediate effects rather than long-term utility. These include healing items like Bandages and First Aid Kits that restore Injury, status cures such as Antidotes and Cure-Alls that remove poison or other negative effects, and support consumables like Heat Packs, Aloe Vera, or Sunscreen that counter environmental damage such as cold, heat, or sunburn. There are also special consumables like Remedy Fungus, which creates a healing cloud, and temporary buff items that restore stamina or clear multiple effects at once. Consumables are usually found in luggage, around campfires, or as rare drops, and using them at the right moment can save a run.


For Items, click [[:Category:Items|here.]]</text></revision>
  </page>
  <page>
    <title>Category:Deployable</title>
    <ns>14</ns>
    <id>2404</id>
    <revision><id>7912</id><timestamp>2026-01-04T09:52:02Z</timestamp><text>In PEAK, deployables are items you can place or use in the world to create climbing aids, platforms, and rest points that help you traverse the mountain more safely and efficiently. Common deployables include Rope Spools and Anti-Rope Spools, which drop 12.5 m of rope downward or upward that players can climb to save stamina; Rope Cannons and Anti-Rope Cannons, which shoot a rope anchor that creates a climbable rope from a distance; Chain Launcher (Chain Cannon), which deploys a horizontal chain you can climb like a vine for team traversal; Piton, which you place on walls as a stamina-recovering handhold mid-climb; Shelf Fungus, throwable mushrooms that create temporary platforms; and Magic Beans, which grow into tall climbable stalks when thrown onto surfaces. These deployable tools are essential for building routes, creating safe resting spots, and overcoming difficult terrain throughout your climb.</text></revision>
  </page>
  <page>
    <title>Category:Leaks</title>
    <ns>14</ns>
    <id>2405</id>
    <revision><id>7916</id><timestamp>2026-01-04T15:52:32Z</timestamp><text>{{Delete|reason=Information on the page already present in [[Unused content]]; no items currently use the category.}}

In PEAK, there are leaked and unreleased items that players have discovered in the game’s files or that were teased by the devs before being fully added. These aren’t normally obtainable in standard gameplay yet, but they give a hint of future or unused content: things like Bounce Shrooms, which launch you a few meters into the air when thrown against a surface; Matchbox, which the community speculates might be used to start fires on-the-go; Wonderberry, a colored fruit sprite that doesn’t currently have stats; Strange Gem, found behind the summit with unknown effects; and odd variants like Energy Elixir and Evil Lollipop that exist in the files but aren’t active in the live game.


These “leak” items mostly come from the PEAK wiki’s [[unused content]] list and community discoveries of hidden assets, and they suggest what might be added or experimented with in future updates even if they’re currently non-functional or purely visual.


(Because this is based on files or data not used in normal gameplay, exact effects aren’t always fully known and some may never be added officially.)</text></revision>
  </page>
